# Formatting is for code. Prose and frozen artefacts keep their hand-set shape.

# The product prototypes are hand-built, self-contained HTML and are design
# artefacts, not code. Reformatting them creates six-hundred-line diffs on
# files whose whole value is that a person shaped them deliberately.
docs/prototype/

# The schema map is the same kind of artefact: one hand-built HTML file whose
# layout carries meaning. Prettier reflows it into six hundred changed lines
# and breaks the shapes tests/schema-map.test.ts reads it by.
docs/schema-map.html

# The walkthrough's diagrams are the same kind again: hand-set HTML pages that
# are screenshotted into the PDF, so a reflow moves nothing but the diff.
docs/walkthrough/diagrams/

# Documentation is hand-wrapped prose; a reflow is churn, not a fix.
*.md

# Generated or machine-owned.
package-lock.json
.next/
node_modules/
next-env.d.ts

# Presentations are slides as they were shown, fonts and data included. A
# reflow would change a record, not fix code.
docs/presentations/
